---
title: Hot Clam Appetizers
author: Mildred McKinzie
category: Appetizers & Dips
source: Loving Memories of Mildred
---

@cream cheese{1%3-oz pkg}
@finely minced onions{2%tsp}
@Worcestershire sauce{3/4%tsp}
@minced clams{1%can}
@salt{1%Dash}
@salt{1/4%tsp}

Drain clams. Whip cream cheese with a fork. Add remaining ingredients and whip until well combined. Cover and chill at least two hours or overnight. Put a teaspoon on a cracker and place cracker on a cookie sheet. Bake at 300 degrees for 20 minutes. Sprinkle with a bit of paprika for color and serve hot.
